    ("Is dental bonding better than porcelain veneers?", "Bonding is cheaper, faster, and less invasive, but it is less stain-resistant and durable than veneers. Veneers are more expensive and require enamel removal but last longer. The best choice depends on your goals and budget. Our detailed guide to <a href=\"/australia/porcelain-veneers/\">porcelain veneers</a> outlines the differences between the two treatments."),
    ("Can a bonded tooth chip or stain?", "Yes. Composite resin can chip or stain over time. Avoid biting hard objects and limit staining foods and drinks. Regular polishing by your dentist helps maintain the finish. Professional <a href=\"/australia/teeth-whitening/\">teeth whitening options</a> do not lighten composite resin; your dentist can re-polish or replace stained bonding."),
